{
  "name": "PACE BMS (RS232 / RS485, protocol 25)",
  "description": "For PACE-based packs speaking PACE protocol 25 (Jakiper, Easun, Tewaycell, Greenrich, FSP, Eenovance and many rebrands)\n- Wiring: the pack's RS232 port (usually RJ11 / RJ12) through a USB-RS232 adapter, or its RS485 port through a USB-RS485 adapter.\n- Set the address field to the pack's DIP-switch address (usually 1).\n- 9600 baud 8N1; a few packs use 19200.\n- Current: positive=charge, negative=discharge.\n- If the pack does not answer, try the other port: on many packs the RS485 / CAN port is set to an inverter protocol instead.\n- Older protocol 20 packs (e.g. EG4 LifePower4) are not covered by this profile.",
  "protocol": "pace-v25",
  "transport": "rs232",
  "default_unit_id": 1,
  "defaults": {
    "baud": 9600,
    "dataBits": 8,
    "stopBits": 1,
    "parity": "none"
  },
  "metrics": [
